From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:55:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: Skip an HEVC reference the queue no longer
 holds

A stream with a gap, a network stall or a cut, names references whose
pictures were dropped. The DPB setup skipped such an entry under a
WARN_ON: a backtrace any player can raise, five in a burst after one
stall. Skip it with a rate-limited debug line, as H.264 does.
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec_h265.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec_h265.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec_h265.c
index 99b562b51..6465f1a5d 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec_h265.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec_h265.c
@@ -327,8 +327,13 @@ cedrus_dec_h265_frame_info_write_dpb(struct cedrus_context *ctx,
 		struct cedrus_buffer *buffer =
 			cedrus_buffer_picture_find(ctx, dpb[i].timestamp);
 
-		if (WARN_ON(!buffer))
+		/* a stream with a gap names references the queue no longer holds */
+		if (!buffer) {
+			dev_dbg_ratelimited(ctx->proc->dev->dev,
+					    "reference %llu not queued\n",
+					    dpb[i].timestamp);
 			continue;
+		}
 
 		cedrus_dec_h265_frame_info_write_single(ctx, buffer, i,
 							dpb[i].field_pic,
-- 
